    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `a6ff9d2f9`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it. It adds test helpers, tests and one decision file; it changes no planner code, no existing test and no golden. The author's gate is green on this head: the quick gate against the side branch (161 steps, 0 failed), clippy on the two test targets, and the light lane (7 steps, the three new twins pass). The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and ends with `Refs #4154`. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer:\n- The trial merge and the gate base are `origin/side/path-kernel`, not `main`.\n- `crates/motion/tests/kernel_laws.rs` is a new top-level test binary. The body gives the reason (rule **New tests join a directory suite**). Decide if the reason is sufficient.\n- The readings are pins of the present behaviour of the old planners. A reading that breaks a law is marked in the table; it is not a defect of this PR.\n- Check the law marks of the decision file (which entry counts against law 5, which kinds count as named slots for law 6).\n- The fig8 2D Contour case is in the heavy lane without a light twin. The body says why.",
